              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p5-q17-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The 32 red and green lollies represent 80% of the total, so there are 40 lollies altogether.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Red and green lollies make up $100\\%-20\\%=80\\%$ of the packet.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Red and green lollies}&=12+20\\\\\\text{Red and green lollies}&=32\\\\\\text{Total lollies}&=32\\div\\frac{80}{100}\\\\\\text{Total lollies}&=40\\\\\\text{Percentage red}&=\\frac{12}{40}\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Percentage red}&=30\\%\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
